[00:10.97] Those schoolgirl days
[00:15.99] Of telling tales and
[00:18.99] Biting nails are gone
[00:25.79] But in my mind, I know
[00:31.72] They will still live on and on
[00:40.23] But how do you thank someone
[00:43.58] Who has taken you from crayons to perfume
[00:49.95] It isn't easy but I'll try
[00:58.24] If you wanted the sky
[01:00.00] I would write across
[01:02.59] The sky in letters
[01:05.52] That would soar
[01:07.08] A thousand feet high
[01:10.75] To Sir with love
[01:19.52] The time has come
[01:24.81] For closing books and
[01:27.72] Long last looks must end
[01:34.59] And as I leave, I know that
[01:40.87] I am leaving my best friend
[01:49.35] A friend who taught me right from wrong
[01:53.04] And weak from strong
[01:55.01] That's a lot to learn
[01:58.05] What, what can I give you in return?
[02:07.50] If you wanted the moon
[02:09.78] I would try to make a start
[02:12.96] But I would rather you
[02:17.08] Let me give my heart
[02:20.24] To Sir with love
[02:28.08]
